  "body": "An exceptionally rare opportunity to acquire two adjoining freehold properties in one of Auckland's most sought-after coastal suburbs. Positioned in the heart of Murrays Bay, 495 East Coast Road and 495A East Coast Road together offer approximately 1,568sqm (more or less) of elevated freehold land with spectacular sea views, premium school zoning and outstanding future development potential (subject to Council approval).\r\n\r\nWastewater and stormwater infrastructure is available on site, offering a significant advantage for future development (subject to purchasers completing their own due diligence).\r\n\r\nExisting dwellings are currently located on both sites, providing holding income or immediate occupancy while future development plans are explored.\r\n\r\nOpportunities to acquire adjoining coastal sites of this scale are seldom available in today's market. Whether you're an experienced developer, investor or land banker, this is an opportunity worthy of serious consideration.\r\n\r\nProperty Highlights\r\n* Approximately 1,568sqm (more or less) combined freehold landholding\r\n* Two adjoining titles available individually or together\r\n* Elevated position with stunning sea views\r\n* Existing dwellings providing holding flexibility\r\n* Existing wastewater and stormwater infrastructure available on site\r\n* Zoned for Rangitoto College, Murrays Bay Intermediate and Murrays Bay School\r\n* Minutes to beaches, public transport, shopping and motorway access\r\n* Flexible settlement terms available\r\n* Outstanding future development potential (subject to Council approval)\r\n\r\nTalk to Harper or Ray today.\r\n\r\n*Purchaser Notice\r\nThe Purchaser acknowledges that the Vendor has disclosed the 495A East Coast Road as being a leaky home. The property is offered for sale on an \"as is, where is\" basis. To the fullest extent permitted by law, the Purchaser accepts the property in its present condition, and the Vendor's warranties contained in the Agreement for Sale and Purchase shall not apply except where they cannot be excluded by law.\r\n\r\n*Interior photos taken from 495 East Coast Road Murrays Bay",
